"Use the pin names returned by the `gpioinfo` utility. This uses the device-"
"tree data. If the installed OS does not have a device-tree database then the "
"pins will all be called \"unnamed\" (or similar) and this driver can not be "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:107
msgid ""
"A further update to this driver might allow access by index number, but this "
"is not currently supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting permissions problems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:112
msgid ""
"If \"access denied\" messages are returned on loading the driver, try the "
"following recipe: (Should not be needed for Raspbian, and will need to be "
"modified to match the actual GPIO chip name on non-Pi platforms)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:114
msgid "Create a new group `gpio` with the command"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:117
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "sudo groupadd gpio\n"
msgstr "sudo gedit\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:122
msgid ""
"Then to setup permissions for the \"gpio\" group, create a file called `90-"
"gpio-access` in the `/etc/udev/rules.d/` directory with the following "
"contents (this is copied from the Raspbian install)"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:132
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SUBSYSTEM==\"bcm2835-gpiomem\", GROUP=\"gpio\", MODE=\"0660\"\n"
"SUBSYSTEM==\"gpio\", GROUP=\"gpio\", MODE=\"0660\"\n"
"SUBSYSTEM==\"gpio*\", PROGRAM=\"/bin/sh -c '\\\n"
"\tchown -R root:gpio /sys/class/gpio && chmod -R 770 /sys/class/gpio;\\\n"
"\tchown -R root:gpio /sys/devices/virtual/gpio &&\\\n"
"\tchmod -R 770 /sys/devices/virtual/gpio;\\\n"
"\tchown -R root:gpio /sys$devpath && chmod -R 770 /sys$devpath\\\n"
"'\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:138
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SUBSYSTEM==\"pwm*\", PROGRAM=\"/bin/sh -c '\\\n"
"\tchown -R root:gpio /sys/class/pwm && chmod -R 770 /sys/class/pwm;\\\n"
"\tchown -R root:gpio /sys/devices/platform/soc/*.pwm/pwm/pwmchip* &&\\\n"
"\tchmod -R 770 /sys/devices/platform/soc/*.pwm/pwm/pwmchip*\\\n"
"'\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:141
msgid "Add the user who runs LinuxCNC to the `gpio` group with"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/hal_gpio.adoc:144
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo usermod -aG gpio <username>\n"
msgstr ""

