#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:110
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Pluto Servo"
msgstr "pluto_servo"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:116
msgid ""
"The pluto_servo system is suitable for control of a 4-axis CNC mill with "
"servo motors, a 3-axis mill with PWM spindle control, a lathe with spindle "
"encoder, etc. The large number of inputs allows a full set of limit switches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:118
msgid "This driver features:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:123
msgid ""
"4 quadrature channels with 40 MHz sample rate. The counters operate in '4x' "
"mode. The maximum useful quadrature rate is 8191 counts per LinuxCNC servo "
"cycle, or about 8 MHz for LinuxCNC's default 1 ms servo rate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:126
msgid ""
"4 PWM channels, 'up/down' or 'pwm+dir' style. 4095 duty cycles from -100% to "
"+100%, including 0%. The PWM period is approximately 19.5 kHz (40 MHz / "
"2047). A PDM-like mode is also available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:129
msgid ""
"18 digital outputs: 10 dedicated, 8 shared with PWM functions.  (Example: A "
"lathe with unidirectional PWM spindle control may use 13 total digital "
"outputs)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:132
msgid ""
"20 digital inputs: 8 dedicated, 12 shared with Quadrature functions.  "
"(Example: A lathe with index pulse only on the spindle may use 13 total "
"digital inputs.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:135
msgid ""
"EPP communication with the PC. The EPP communication typically takes around "
"100 µs on machines tested so far, enabling servo rates above 1 kHz."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:143
msgid ""
"'UPx' - The 'up' (up/down mode) or 'pwm' (pwm+direction mode) signal from "
"PWM generator X. May be used as a digital output if the corresponding PWM "
"channel is unused, or the output on the channel is always negative. The "
"corresponding digital output invert may be set to TRUE to make UPx active "
"low rather than active high."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:148
msgid ""
"'DNx' - The 'down' (up/down mode) or 'direction' (pwm+direction mode)  "
"signal from PWM generator X. May be used as a digital output if the "
"corresponding PWM channel is unused, or the output on the channel is never "
"negative. The corresponding digital output invert may be set to TRUE to make "
"DNx active low rather than active high."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:150
msgid ""
"'QAx, QBx' - The A and B signals for Quadrature counter X. May be used as a "
"digital input if the corresponding quadrature channel is unused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:153
msgid ""
"'QZx' - The Z (index) signal for quadrature counter X. May be used as a "
"digital input if the index feature of the corresponding quadrature channel "
"is unused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:154 src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:240
msgid "'INx' - Dedicated digital input #x"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:155 src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:241
msgid "'OUTx' - Dedicated digital output #x"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:156 src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:242
msgid "'GND' - Ground"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:157 src/drivers/pluto-p.adoc:243
msgid "'VCC' - +3.3V regulated DC"
msgstr ""

