#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "VFS11 VFD Driver"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:12
msgid ""
"This is a non-realtime HAL program to control the S11 series of VFDs from "
"Toshiba."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:16
msgid ""
"vfs11_vfd supports serial and TCP connections.  Serial connections may be "
"RS232 or RS485. RS485 is supported in full- and half-duplex mode.  TCP "
"connections may be passive (wait for incoming connection), or active "
"outgoing connections, which may be useful to connect to TCP-based devices or "
"through a terminal server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:18
msgid ""
"Regardless of the connection type, vfs11_vfd operates as a Modbus master."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:24
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "loadusr -Wn spindle-vfd vfs11_vfd -n spindle-vfd\n"
msgstr "loadusr -Wn spindle gs2_vfd -n spindle\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:27
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The above command says: loadusr, wait for named to load, component "
"vfs11_vfd, named spindle-vfd"
msgstr ""
"Esto ultimo significa: 'loadusr espera la carga del componente spindle, que "
"es un componente gs2_vfd, nombrado como spindle'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:31
msgid ""
"'vfs11_vfd' is mostly configured through INI file options. The command line "
"options are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:33
msgid "'-n or --name <halname>' : set the HAL component name"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:35
msgid ""
"'-I or --ini <inifilename>' : take configuration from this INI file.  "
"Defaults to environment variable INI_FILE_NAME."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:36
msgid ""
"'-S or --section <section name>' : take configuration from this section in "
"the INI file. Defaults to 'VFS11'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:37
msgid "'-d or --debug' enable debug messages on console output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:38
msgid "'-m or --modbus-debug' enable modbus messages on console output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:39
msgid "'-r or --report-device' report device properties on console at startup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:42
msgid ""
"Debugging can be toggled by sending a USR1 signal to the vfs11_vfd process.  "
"Modbus debugging can be toggled by sending a USR2 signal to vfs11_vfd "
"process (example: +kill -USR1 \\`pidof vfs11_vfd`+)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:49 src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:125
msgid ""
"Where <n> is +vfs11_vfd+ or the name given during loading with the -n option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:51
msgid ""
"'<n>.acceleration-pattern' (bit, in) when true, set acceleration and "
"deceleration times as defined in registers F500 and F501 respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:52
msgid "Used in PID loops to choose shorter ramp times to avoid oscillation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:55
msgid ""
"'<n>.alarm-code' (s32, out) non-zero if drive is in alarmed state.  Bitmap "
"describing alarm information (see register FC91 description).  Use err-reset "
"(see below) to clear the alarm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:57
msgid ""
"'<n>.at-speed' (bit, out)  when drive is at commanded speed (see speed-"
"tolerance below)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:59
msgid "'<n>.current-load-percentage' (float, out)  reported from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:61
msgid ""
"'<n>.dc-brake' (bit, in)  engage the DC brake. Also turns off spindle-on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:64
msgid ""
"'<n>.enable' (bit, in)  enable the VFD.  If false, all operating parameters "
"are still read but control is released and panel control is enabled (subject "
"to VFD setup)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:67
msgid ""
"'<n>.err-reset' (bit, in)  reset errors (alarms a.k.a Trip and e-stop "
"status).  Resetting the VFD may cause a 2-second delay until it's rebooted "
"and Modbus is up again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:70
msgid ""
"'<n>.estop' (bit, in)  put the VFD into emergency-stopped status.  No "
"operation possible until cleared with err-reset or powercycling."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:72
msgid ""
"'<n>.frequency-command' (float, out)  current target frequency in Hz as set "
"through speed-command (which is in RPM), from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:74
msgid "'<n>.frequency-out' (float, out)  current output frequency of the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:76
msgid ""
"'<n>.inverter-load-percentage' (float, out)  current load report from VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:79
msgid ""
"'<n>.is-e-stopped' (bit, out)  the VFD is in emergency stop status (blinking "
"\"E\" on panel).  Use err-reset to reboot the VFD and clear the e- stop "
"status."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:81
msgid "'<n>.is-stopped' (bit, out)  true when the VFD reports 0 Hz output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:88
msgid ""
"'<n>.max-rpm' (float, R)  actual RPM limit based on maximum frequency the "
"VFD may generate, and the motors nameplate values.  For instance, if "
"nameplate-HZ is 50, and nameplate-RPM_ is 1410, but the VFD may generate up "
"to 80 Hz, then max-rpm would read as 2256 (80*1410/50).  The frequency limit "
"is read from the VFD at startup.  To increase the upper frequency limit, the "
"UL and FH parameters must be changed on the panel.  See the VF-S11 manual "
"for instructions how to set the maximum frequency."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:90
msgid ""
"'<n>.modbus-ok' (bit, out)  true when the Modbus session is successfully "
"established and the last 10 transactions returned without error."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:92
msgid "'<n>.motor-RPM' (float, out)  estimated current RPM value, from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:94
msgid "'<n>.output-current-percentage' (float, out)  from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:96
msgid "'<n>.output-voltage-percentage' (float, out)  from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:98
msgid "'<n>.output-voltage' (float, out)  from the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:100
msgid ""
"'<n>.speed-command' (float, in)  speed sent to VFD in RPM. It is an error to "
"send a speed faster than the Motor Max RPM as set in the VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:102
msgid "'<n>.spindle-fwd' (bit, in)  1 for FWD and 0 for REV, sent to VFD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:104
msgid ""
"'<n>.spindle-on' (bit, in)  1 for ON and 0 for OFF sent to VFD, only on when "
"running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:106
msgid ""
"'<n>.spindle-rev' (bit, in)  1 for ON and 0 for OFF, only on when running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:111
msgid ""
"'<n>.jog-mode' (bit, in)  1 for ON and 0 for OFF, enables the VF-S11 'jog "
"mode'.  Speed control is disabled, and the output frequency is determined by "
"register F262 (preset to 5 Hz).  This might be useful for spindle "
"orientation.  In normal mode, the VFD shuts off if the frequency drops below "
"12 Hz."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:114
msgid ""
"'<n>.status' (s32, out)  Drive Status of the VFD (see the TOSVERT VF-S11 "
"Communications Function Instruction Manual, register FD01).  A bitmap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:116
msgid "'<n>.trip-code' (s32, out)  trip code if VF-S11 is in tripped state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:118
msgid ""
"'<n>.error-count' (s32, out)  number of Modbus transactions which returned "
"an error"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:121
msgid ""
"'<n>.max-speed' (bit, in)  ignore the loop-time parameter and run Modbus at "
"maximum speed, at the expense of higher CPU usage.  Suggested use during "
"spindle positioning."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:128
msgid "'<n>.frequency-limit' (float, RO)  upper limit read from VFD setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:130
msgid ""
"'<n>.loop-time' (float, RW)  how often the Modbus is polled (default "
"interval 0.1 seconds)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:132
msgid ""
"'<n>.nameplate-HZ' (float, RW)  Nameplate Hz of motor (default 50). Used to "
"calculate target frequency (together with nameplate-RPM ) for a target RPM "
"value as given by speed-command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:134
msgid "'<n>.nameplate-RPM' (float, RW)  Nameplate RPM of motor (default 1410)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:136
msgid ""
"'<n>.rpm-limit' (float, RW)  do-not-exceed soft limit for motor RPM "
"(defaults to nameplate-RPM )."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:139
msgid ""
"'<n>.tolerance' (float, RW)  speed tolerance (default 0.01) for determining "
"whether spindle is at speed (0.01 meaning: Output frequency is within 1% of "
"target frequency)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:140
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "INI file configuration"
msgstr "Configuración de git"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:144
msgid ""
"This lists all options understood by vfs11_vfd.  Typical setups for RS-232, "
"RS-485 and TCP can be found in 'src/hal/user_comps/vfs11_vfd/*.ini'."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[VFS11]\n"
"# serial connection\n"
"TYPE=rtu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:153
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# serial port\n"
"DEVICE=/dev/ttyS0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:156
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# TCP server - wait for incoming connection\n"
"TYPE=tcpserver\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:159
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# tcp portnumber for TYPE=tcpserver or tcpclient\n"
"PORT=1502\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# TCP client - active outgoing connection\n"
"TYPE=tcpclient\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:165
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# destination to connect to if TYPE=tcpclient\n"
"TCPDEST=192.168.1.1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#---------- meaningful only if TYPE=rtu -------\n"
"# serial device detail\n"
"# 5 6 7 8\n"
"BITS= 5\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# even odd none\n"
"PARITY=none\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:176
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 110, 300, 600, 1200, 2400, 4800, 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200\n"
"BAUD=19200\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:179
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 1 2\n"
"STOPBITS=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#rs232 rs485\n"
"SERIAL_MODE=rs485\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:189
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# up down none\n"
"# this feature might not work with a stock Ubuntu\n"
"# libmodbus5/libmodbus-dev package, and generate a warning\n"
"# execution will continue as if RTS_MODE=up were given.\n"
"RTS_MODE=up\n"
"#---------------------\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:195
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# modbus timers in seconds\n"
"# inter-character timer\n"
"BYTE_TIMEOUT=0.5\n"
"# packet timer\n"
"RESPONSE_TIMEOUT=0.5\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:198
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# target modbus ID\n"
"TARGET=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# on I/O failure, try to reconnect after sleeping\n"
"# for RECONNECT_DELAY seconds\n"
"RECONNECT_DELAY=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:207
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# misc. parameters\n"
"DEBUG=10\n"
"MODBUS_DEBUG=0\n"
"POLLCYCLES=10\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:218
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#\n"
"# example usage of the VF-S11 VFD driver\n"
"#\n"
"#\n"
"loadusr -Wn spindle-vfd vfs11_vfd -n spindle-vfd\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:222
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the spindle direction pins to the VFD\n"
"net vfs11-fwd spindle-vfd.spindle-fwd <= spindle.0.forward\n"
"net vfs11-rev spindle-vfd.spindle-rev <= spindle.0.reverse\n"
msgstr ""
"# conecte el pin de dirección del husillo al GS2\n"
"net gs2-fwd spindle-vfd.spindle-fwd <= spindle.N.forward\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:225
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the spindle on pin to the VF-S11\n"
"net vfs11-run spindle-vfd.spindle-on <= spindle.0.on\n"
msgstr ""
"# conecte el pin de arranque del husillo al GS2\n"
"net gs2-run spindle-vfd.spindle-on <= spindle.N.on\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:228
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the VF-S11 at speed to the motion at speed\n"
"net vfs11-at-speed spindle.0.at-speed <= spindle-vfd.at-speed\n"
msgstr ""
"# conecte el GS2 a velocidad al movimiento a velocidad\n"
"net gs2-at-speed spindle.N.at-speed <= spindle-vfd.at-speed\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:231
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the spindle RPM to the VF-S11\n"
"net vfs11-RPM spindle-vfd.speed-command <= spindle.0.speed-out\n"
msgstr ""
"# conecte RPM de husillo al GS2\n"
"net gs2-RPM spindle-vfd.speed-command <= spindle.N.speed-out\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:236
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# connect the VF-S11 DC brake\n"
"# since this draws power during spindle off, the dc-brake pin would\n"
"# better be driven by a monoflop which triggers on spindle-on falling edge\n"
"#net vfs11-spindle-brake spindle.N.brake => spindle-vfd.dc-brake\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:240
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# to use the VFS11 jog mode for spindle orient\n"
"# see orient.9 and motion.9\n"
"net spindle-orient spindle.0.orient spindle-vfd.max-speed spindle-vfd.jog-mode\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:243
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# take precedence over control panel\n"
"setp spindle-vfd.enable 1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:245
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Panel operation"
msgstr "Configuración del panel"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:252
msgid ""
"The vfs11_vfd driver takes precedence over panel control while it is enabled "
"(see 'enable' pin), effectively disabling the panel.  Clearing the 'enable' "
"pin re-enables the panel.  Pins and parameters can still be set, but will "
"not be written to the VFD untile the 'enable' pin is set.  Operating "
"parameters are still read while bus control is disabled.  Exiting the "
"vfs11_vfd driver in a controlled way will release the VFD from the bus and "
"restore panel control."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:255
msgid ""
"See the LinuxCNC Integrators Manual for more information.  For a detailed "
"register description of the Toshiba VFDs, see the \"TOSVERT VF-S11 "
"Communications Function Instruction Manual\" (Toshiba document number "
"E6581222) and the \"TOSVERT VF-S11 Instruction manual\" (Toshiba document "
"number E6581158)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error Recovery"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:259
msgid ""
"+vfs11_vfd+ recovers from I/O errors as follows: First, all HAL pins are set "
"to default values, and the driver will sleep for +RECONNECT_DELAY+ seconds "
"(default 1 second)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:261
msgid "Serial (+TYPE=rtu+) mode: on error, close and reopen the serial port."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:262
msgid ""
"TCP server (+TYPE=tcpserver+) mode: on losing the TCP connection, the driver "
"will go back to listen for incoming connections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:263
msgid ""
"TCP client (+TYPE=tcpclient+) mode: on losing the TCP connection, the driver "
"will reconnect to 'TCPDEST:PORTNO'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:264
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuring the VFS11 VFD for Modbus usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:274
msgid ""
"The VF-S11 has an RJ-45 jack for serial communication.  Unfortunately, it "
"does not have a standard RS-232 plug and logic levels.  The Toshiba-"
"recommended way is: connect the USB001Z USB-to-serial conversion unit to the "
"drive, and plug the USB port into the PC.  A cheaper alternative is a "
"homebrew interface ( https://git.mah.priv.at/gitweb/vfs11-vfd.git/blob_plain/"
"refs/heads/f12-prod:/VFS11-RJ45_e.pdf[hints from Toshiba support], https://"
"git.mah.priv.at/gitweb/vfs11-vfd.git/blob_plain/refs/heads/f12-prod:/vfs11-"
"rs232.pdf[circuit diagram])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:276
msgid "Note: the 24V output from the VFD has no short-circuit protection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:278
msgid ""
"Serial port factory defaults are 9600/8/1/even, the protocol defaults to the "
"proprietary \"Toshiba Inverter Protocol\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
