msgstr "net signal-name motion.digital-in-00 <= parport.0.pin10-in\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/gcode/m-code.adoc:423
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "M67 Analog Output, Synchronized(((M67 Analog Output, Synchronized)))"
msgstr "M67 Salida analógica, sincronizada(((M67 Analog Output, Synchronized)))"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gcode/m-code.adoc:428
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "M67 E- Q-\n"
msgstr "M67 E- Q-\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gcode/m-code.adoc:431
#, fuzzy
msgid "'M67' - set an analog output synchronized with motion."
msgstr "'M67' - establece una salida analógica sincronizada con el movimiento."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gcode/m-code.adoc:432
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'E-' - output number ranging from 0 to 3 (Adjustable from motmod argument "
"num_aio)"
msgstr "'E-' - número de salida que va de 0 a 3."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gcode/m-code.adoc:433 src/gcode/m-code.adoc:459
#, fuzzy
msgid "'Q-' - is the value to set (set to 0 to turn off)."
msgstr "'Q-' - es el valor a configurar (establecer a 0 para desactivar)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gcode/m-code.adoc:439
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The actual change of the specified outputs will happen at the beginning of "
"the next motion command. If there is no subsequent motion command, the "
"queued output changes won't happen. It's best to always program a motion G-"
"code (G0, G1, etc) right after the M67. M67 functions the same as M62-63."
