#. type: Title ==
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:7
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "The Software"
msgstr "El software"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:12
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"LinuxCNC (the Enhanced Machine Control) is a software system for computer "
"control of machine tools such as milling machines and lathes, robots such as "
"puma and scara and other computer controlled machines up to 9 axes."
msgstr ""
"LinuxCNC (“Enhanced Machine Control” o Control de Máquina Mejorado) es un "
"sistema de software para control de máquinas herramientas como fresadoras y "
"tornos, robots tipos puma y scara y otras máquinas controladas por "
"computadora, de hasta 9 ejes."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:15
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"LinuxCNC is free software with open source code. Current versions of "
"LinuxCNC are entirely licensed under the GNU General Public License and "
"Lesser GNU General Public License (GPL and LGPL)."
msgstr ""
"LinuxCNC es un software gratuito con código fuente abierto. Las versiones "
"actuales de LinuxCNC están completamente licenciadas bajo la Licencia "
"Pública General de GNU (GPL) y Lesser GNU General Public License (LGPL)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:16
#, fuzzy
msgid "LinuxCNC provides:"
msgstr "LinuxCNC proporciona:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:17
#, fuzzy
msgid "easy discovery and testing without installation with the LiveCD,"
msgstr "easy discovery and testing without installation with the LiveCD"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:18
#, fuzzy
msgid "easy installation from the Live CD,"
msgstr "instalación fácil con un Live-CD"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:20
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"easy to use graphical configuration wizards to rapidly create a "
"configuration specific to the machine,"
msgstr ""
"Easy to use graphical configuration wizards to rapidly create a "
"configuration specific to the machine"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:21
msgid ""
"directly available as regular packages of recent releases of Debian (since "
"Bookworm) and Ubuntu (since Kinetic Kudu),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:22
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"a graphical user interface (actually several interfaces to choose from),"
msgstr ""
"una interfaz gráfica de usuario (en realidad, varias interfaces entre las "
"que elegir)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:23
#, fuzzy
msgid "a graphical interface creation tool (Glade),"
msgstr "A graphical interface creation tool (GladeVCP)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:25
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"an interpreter for 'G-code' (the RS-274 machine tool programming language),"
msgstr ""
"un intérprete para 'código G' (lenguaje de programación de máquinas "
"herramienta RS-274)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:26
#, fuzzy
msgid "a realtime motion planning system with look-ahead,"
msgstr ""
"un sistema de planificación de movimiento en tiempo real con análisis de "
"instrucción siguiente"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:27
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"operation of low-level machine electronics such as sensors and motor drives,"
msgstr ""
"operación de la electrónica de bajo nivel de la máquina, como sensores y "
"motores"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:28
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"an easy to use 'breadboard' layer for quickly creating a unique "
"configuration for your machine,"
msgstr ""
"una capa que actua como 'breadboard', fácil de usar, para crear rápidamente "
"una configuración unica para su máquina"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:29
#, fuzzy
msgid "a software PLC programmable with ladder diagrams."
msgstr "un PLC en software, programable, con diagramas de escalera"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:31
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It does not provide drawing (CAD - Computer Aided Design) or G-code "
"generation from the drawing (CAM - Computer Automated Manufacturing) "
"functions."
msgstr ""
"No proporciona herramientas de dibujo (CAD - Diseño asistido por "
"computadora) ni funciones de generación de código G a partir de dibujos (CAM "
"- Fabricación automatizada por computadora)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:32
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It can simultaneously move up to 9 axes and supports a variety of interfaces."
msgstr ""
"Puede mover simultáneamente hasta 9 ejes y admite una variedad de interfaces"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:35
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The control can operate true servos (analog or PWM) with the feedback loop "
"closed by the LinuxCNC software at the computer, or open loop with step-"
"servos or stepper motors."
msgstr ""
"El control puede operar servos verdaderos (analógicos o PWM) con "
"retroalimentación de bucle cerrado por el software LinuxCNC en la "
"computadora, o bucle abierto, con servomotores o motores paso a paso."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:39
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Motion control features include: cutter radius and length compensation, path "
"deviation limited to a specified tolerance, lathe threading, synchronized "
"axis motion, adaptive feedrate, operator feed override, and constant "
"velocity control."
msgstr ""
"Las características de control de movimiento incluyen: compensación del "
"radio de corte y longitud de herramienta, desviación de trayectoria limitada "
"a una tolerancia especificada, roscado en torno, movimientos de eje "
"sincronizados, avance adaptativo, control de ajuste de avance por el "
"operador y control de velocidad constante."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:43
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Support for non-Cartesian motion systems is provided via custom kinematics "
"modules. Available architectures include hexapods (Stewart platforms and "
"similar concepts) and systems with rotary joints to provide motion such as "
"PUMA or SCARA robots."
msgstr ""
"Soporte para sistemas de movimiento no cartesianos, a través de módulos "
"cinemáticos personalizados.  Las arquitecturas disponibles incluyen "
"hexapodos (plataformas Stewart y conceptos similares) y sistemas con "
"articulaciones rotativas para proporcionar movimiento como robots PUMA o "
"SCARA."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/getting-started/about-linuxcnc.adoc:44
#, fuzzy
msgid "LinuxCNC runs on Linux using real time extensions."
msgstr "LinuxCNC se ejecuta en Linux usando extensiones en tiempo real."

