#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:657
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Z level compensation"
msgstr "Compensacion de Herramientas"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:660
msgid ""
"QtDragon_hd can be set up to probe and compensate for Z level height changes "
"by utilizing the external program 'G-code Ripper'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:663 src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1052
msgid "This is only available in the QtDragon_hd version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:668
msgid ""
"Z level compensation is a bed levelling/distortion correction function "
"typically used in 3D printing or engraving.  It uses a HAL non-realtime "
"component which utilizes the external offsets feature of LinuxCNC.  The "
"component has a HAL pin that specifies an interpolation type, which must be "
"one of cubic, linear or nearest (0, 1, 2 respectively).  If none is "
"specified or if an invalid number is specified, the default is assumed to be "
"cubic."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:673
msgid ""
"When Z LEVEL COMP is enabled, the compensation component reads a probe data "
"file, which must be called 'probe_points.txt'.  The file can be modified or "
"updated at any time while compensation is disabled.  When next enabled, the "
"file will be reread and the compensation map is recalculated.  This file is "
"expected to be in the configuration directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:676
msgid ""
"The probe data file is generated by a probing program, which itself is "
"generated by an external python program called `gcode_ripper`, which can be "
"launched from the file manager tab using the 'G-code Ripper' button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:677
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using G-code Ripper for Z level Compensation"
msgstr ""

