#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:925
msgid ""
"You can use a conductive touch plate or equivalent to auto touch off (zero "
"the user coordinate) for the Z position of a tool.  There must be a tool "
"loaded prior to probing.  In the tool tab or settings tab, set the touch "
"plate height, search and probe velocity and max. probing distance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:930
msgid ""
"When using a conductive plate the search and probe velocity should be the "
"same and slow.  If using a tool setter that has spring loaded travel then "
"you can set search velocity faster.  LinuxCNC ramps speed down at the "
"maximum acceleration rate, so there can be travel after the probe trip if "
"the speed is set to high."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:937
msgid ""
"Place the plate on top of the surface you wish to zero Z on.  Connect the "
"probe input wire to the tool (if using a conductive plate).  There is a LED "
"to confirm the probe connection is reliable prior to probing.  Move the tool "
"manually within the max probe distance.  Press the 'Touch Plate' button.  "
"The machine will probe down twice and the current user offset (G5X) will be "
"zeroed at the bottom of the plate by calculation from the touchplate height "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:943
msgid ""
"QtDragon can be setup to do integrated auto tool measurement using the Versa "
"Probe widget and remap code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:945
msgid "This feature assumes the use of two probes in concert:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:947
msgid ""
"A tool switch sensor, fixed somewhere on the machine (sometimes called a "
"tool-setter), and"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:948
msgid ""
"A spindle probe that is installed temporarily at the beginning of the job "
"(sometimes called an xyz probe or a Renishaw probe)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:950
msgid ""
"These techniques are useful for machines that do not have repeatable tool "
"holders and do not have automatic tool changing devices. (For machines with "
"repeatable tool holders, see the section on <<sub:touch-plate,measuring tool "
"length>>. For machines with automatic tool changing devices, consult work "
"done under the linuxcnc repository at configs/sim/axis/remap/rack-toolchange)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:952
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To use this feature, you will need to do some additional settings and you "
"may want to use the offered HAL pins to get values in your own ngc remap "
"procedure. Those settings are covered later in the section."
msgstr ""
"Gmoccapy ofrece una medición automática integrada de herramientas. Para usar "
"esta característica, usted tendrá que hacer algunos ajustes adicionales y es "
"posible que desee utilizar el pin hal que se ofrece para obtener valores en "
"su propio procedimiento ngc de remapeo."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:954
msgid ""
"First, this document covers how to use this technique. Second, this document "
"covers how to set up for this technique at the beginning of a production run."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:955
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow Overview"
msgstr "Descripción general"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:958
msgid "A detailed workflow walkthrough follows this overview."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:967
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setup steps include: +\n"
" +\n"
"Entering the probe velocities on the versa probe settings page. +\n"
"Enabling \"Use Tool Measurement\" on the Versa Probe tab. +\n"
"Enabling \"Use Tool Sensor\" under Settings. +\n"
" +\n"
"When fist setting up auto tool measurement, please use caution until you confirm tool change and probe locations - it is easy to break a tool/probe. Abort will be honoured while the probe is in motion.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:969
msgid ""
"Tool Measurement in QtDragon is organized into the following steps which "
"will be explained in more detail in the following section:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:971
msgid ""
"Zero the probe tool by measuring the tool setter with the spindle probe "
"installed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:973
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Measure the height of your block from the base, where your tool switch is "
"located, to the upper face of the block (including chuck etc.)."
msgstr ""
"mida la altura de su bloque desde la base donde está ubicado su interruptor "
"de herramienta a la cara superior del bloque (incluida mordaza, etc.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:974
msgid "In the Versa probe tab, enter the measured value for block height."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:976
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Auto tool measurement"
msgstr "Medición automática de herramientas"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:981
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the first given tool change the tool will be measured and the offset "
"will be set automatically to fit the block height.  The advantage of this "
"way is, that you do not need a reference tool."
msgstr ""
"Con el primer cambio de herramienta, la herramienta se medirá y el offset se "
"configura automáticamente para adaptarse a la altura del bloque. La ventaja "
"de gmoccapy es que no se necesita una herramienta de referencia."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:984
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Your program must contain a tool change at the beginning. The tool will be "
"measured, even it has been used before, so there is no danger if the block "
"height has changed. There are several videos on you tube that demonstrate "
"the technique using GMOCCAPY. The GMOCCAPY screen pioneered the technique."
msgstr ""
"¡Su programa debe contener un cambio de herramienta al principio! La "
"herramienta será medida, incluso se ha utilizado antes, por lo que no hay "
"peligro si la altura del bloque ha cambiado. Hay varios videos que muestran "
"la manera de hacerlo en Youtube."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:986
msgid ""
"The sequence of events (using the default files in the default setting):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:988
msgid "Rapid move in Z to position defined in the INI's [TOOL_CHANGE] Z"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:989
msgid "Rapid move in X and Y to number defined in INI's [TOOL_CHANGE] X and Y"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:990
msgid ""
"Perform normal M6 tool change: ie, stop spindle, send message to user to "
"change the tool"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:991
msgid ""
"Rapid move in X and Y to position defined in the INI's [VERSA_TOOLSETTER] X "
"and Y"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:992
msgid ""
"Rapid move down in Z to position defined in the INI's [VERSA_TOOLSETTER] Z"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:993
msgid ""
"Probe down in Z to maximum defined in the INI's [VERSA_TOOLSETTER] MAXPROBE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:994
msgid ""
"Changes the offset of the current work coordinate system to match the "
"difference between the previous tool and the currently measured tool"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:995
msgid ""
"Rapid move up in Z to position defined in the INI's [VERSA_TOOLSETTER] "
"Z_MAX_CLEAR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:996
msgid "Rapid move to the X Y position when the tool change was called"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:997
msgid "Rapid move down to the Z position when the tool change was called"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1002
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [TOOL_CHANGE] Z position should be high enough so the tool will not hit the tool probe when moving to the [VERSA_TOOLSETTER] X and Y position. +\n"
"  +\n"
"MAXPROBE distance needs to be high enough for the tool to touch the probe.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1003
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Detailed Workflow Example"
msgstr "Ejemplo detallado (RV-6SL)"

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1005
#, no-wrap
msgid "One Time Setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1008
msgid ""
"The following setups need only be done once as long as they remain in effect:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1010
msgid ""
"Under Probe Tool Screens: Insure reasonable values for \"Rapid\" and "
"\"Search,\" these are the speeds at which the probing will be performed and "
"are in machine units per minute. +"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1011
msgid ""
"Under Probe Tool Screens: insure that \"Tool Measure\" is enabled (this is a "
"button that must be highlighted)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1012
msgid ""
"Under Settings: insure that \"Use Tool Sensor\" is enabled (this is a tick-"
"box that must be checked)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1013
msgid ""
"In the Tool Table: setup a tool for the spindle probe and insure that its Z "
"offset is set to zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1016
msgid ""
"It is possible to use a non-zero tool length for the tool probe, but this "
"requires extra steps and is easy to make mistakes. The following procedure "
"assumes a zero tool probe length."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1017
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Procedure before starting a program"
msgstr "P or p = pause program"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1020
msgid ""
"The following setup is done before beginning a program that has M6 tool "
"change commands inside it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1022
msgid "Physically load the spindle probe into the spindle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1023
msgid ""
"Logically load the spindle probe into the spindle with the M61 Qx command "
"where x is the number in the tool table for the spindle probe (there is a "
"button inside the tool table tab that can also be used)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1024
msgid ""
"Position to the Toolsetter: Use the button under the Probe Screens for \"Go "
"To Toolsetter\" to position the spindle above the Toolsetter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1025
msgid ""
"Toolsetter Measure: Use the button under the Probe Screens for \"Probe Tool "
"Setter Z Height.\" Note that this will set and display on the Probe Settings "
"screen the \"Probe HT\" value in ABS coordinates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1026
#, fuzzy
msgid "Jog to your workpiece."
msgstr "toque de su pieza en X e Y"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1027
msgid ""
"Workpiece Measure: Use the button under the Probe Screens for \"Probe Z "
"Height of Material:\" this will set and display on the Probe Settings screen "
"the \"Block Ht\" value in ABS coordinates. (Typically, this will now also be "
"the zero Z for your Work Coordinate System)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1028
msgid ""
"Set Work Coordinate System (ie, G54, or other): Use the Probe Tool and "
"whatever probe screen or other method is appropriate to set the X, Y, and Z "
"coordinate system needed for your job."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1029
msgid ""
"If your program begins with a TnM6 command before spinning the spindle, you "
"may leave the spindle probe installed. You may also issue a TnM6 command to "
"change out the spindle probe, and if the program issues the same one, it "
"will skip the tool change."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1032
msgid ""
"Take care not to leave the spindle probe in the spindle if a program may "
"start the spindle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1034
msgid ""
"Once those steps are complete, a program with multiple TnM6 toolchanges can "
"be started and will operate with automatic pauses for manual tool change "
"followed by automated tool measurement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1037
msgid ""
"After probing the new tool length using the tool-setter, this remap code "
"uses a G43 which applies the offset to the Work Coordinate system which was "
"in effect when the M6 command was issued. Because remapping has adjusted the "
"Work Coordinate system by the offset between the previous and the current "
"tool, the tool tip will end up at the same point in space as the tip of the "
"previous tool was when the tool change was called."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/qtdragon.adoc:1038
#, no-wrap
msgid "Work Piece Height Probing in QtDragon_hd"
