msgid ""
"You can also add them directly to the _UI_ - but each dialog must have a "
"unique launch name or you will see multiple dialogs displayed, one after "
"another."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2423
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use dialogs from Python Code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2425
msgid ""
"You can show dialogs directly with _Python code_, but a safer way is to *use "
"`STATUS` messages* to request the dialog to launch and to return the "
"gathered information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2428
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Register to `STATUS` channel*: +\n"
"To set this up, first register to catch the `general` message from `STATUS`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2439
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Add a function to call a dialog*: +\n"
"This function must _build a message `dict` to send to the dialog_. +\n"
"This message will be passed back in the general message with the addition of the _`return` variable_. +\n"
"It is possible to add _extra user information_ to the message.\n"
"The dialog will ignore these and pass them back.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2439
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NAME`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2440
msgid "Launches code name of dialog to show."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2440
#, no-wrap
msgid "`ID`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2441
msgid "A unique id so we process only a dialog that we requested."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2441
#, no-wrap
msgid "`TITLE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2442
#, fuzzy
msgid "The title to use on the dialog."
msgstr "La Ventana de AXIS"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2450
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def show_dialog(self):\n"
"    mess = {'NAME':'ENTRY','ID':'__test1__',\n"
"            'TITLE':'Test Entry'}\n"
"    ACTION.CALL_DIALOG, mess)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2456
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Add a callback function that processes the general message*: +\n"
"Keep in mind this function will _get all general messages_ so the `dict` keynames are not guaranteed to be there.\n"
"Using the `.get()` function and/or using `try`/`except` is advisable.\n"
"This function should:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2457
#, no-wrap
msgid "check the name and id is the same as we sent,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2458
#, no-wrap
msgid "then extract the return value and any user variables.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2469
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# process the STATUS return message\n"
"def return_value(self, w, message):\n"
"    rtn = message.get('RETURN')\n"
"    code = bool(message.get('ID') == '__test1__')\n"
"    name = bool(message.get('NAME') == 'ENTRY')\n"
"    if code and name and not rtn is None:\n"
"        print('Entry return value from {} = {}'.format(code, rtn))\n"
msgstr ""

