msgstr "halrun -U\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*halrun* is a convenience script used to manipulate the HAL (Hardware\n"
"Abstraction Layer) from the command line. When invoked, *halrun*:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:25
msgid ""
"Sets up the realtime environment. Executes a command interpreter (*halcmd* "
"or *haltcl*). (Optionally) runs an interactive session. Tears down the "
"realtime environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:29
msgid ""
"If no filename is specified, an interactive session is started. The session "
"will use *halcmd*(1) unless -T is specified in which case *haltcl*(1) will "
"be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:34
msgid ""
"If a filename is specified and neither the -I nor the -T option is included, "
"the filename will be processed by the command interpreter corresponding to "
"the filename extension (*halcmd* or *haltcl*). After processing, the "
"realtime environment will be torn down."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:39
msgid ""
"If a filename is specified and the -I or -T option is included, the file is "
"processed by the appropriate command interpreter and then an interactive "
"session is started for *halcmd* or *haltcl* according to the -I or -T option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:42
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*halcmd_opts*"
msgstr "Halscope"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:46
msgid ""
"When a .hal file is specified, the *halcmd_opts* are passed to *halcmd*.  "
"See the man page for **halcmd**(1).  When a .tcl file is specified, the only "
"valid options are: -i <INI file> -f <filename[.tcl|.hal]> (alternate means "
"of specifying a file)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:48
msgid "Run an interactive *halcmd* session"
msgstr ""

