#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Sim Configs"
msgstr "Configs"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:262
msgid ""
"The distribution includes several simulation configurations in the directory:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:267
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   /usr/share/doc/linuxcnc/examples/sample-configs/sim/axis/xhc-hb04/\n"
"or for a RIP build:\n"
"   rip_base_dir/configs/sim/axis/xhc-hb04/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:274
msgid ""
"These configurations use a distribution-provided script (xhc-hb04.tcl)  to "
"configure the pendant and make necessary HAL connections according to a "
"number of INI file settings. The script uses an additional HAL component "
"(xhc_hb04_util) to provide common functionality and includes support for a "
"standard method for the start-pause button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:282
msgid ""
"The settings available include: 1) specify button-cfg-file for standard "
"layout1 or layout2 2) select axes (up to 4 axes from set of x y z a b c u v "
"w) 3) implement per-axis filtering coefficients 4) implement per-axis "
"acceleration for mpg jogging 5) implement per-axis scale settings 6) select "
"normal or velocity based jog modes 7) select stepsize sequence 8) option to "
"initialize pin for inch or mm display icon 9)  option to require pendant on "
"startup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:286
msgid ""
"The sim configs illustrate button connections that: 1) connect pendant "
"stepsize-up button to the step input pin. 2) connect buttons to halui.* pins "
"3) connect buttons to motion.* pins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:290
msgid ""
"Another script is included to monitor the pendant and report loss of USB "
"connectivity. See the README and .txt files in the above directory for usage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:296
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Note:* The sim configs use the AXIS GUI but the scripts are available\n"
"with any HAL configuration or GUI. The same scripts can be used to adapt\n"
"the xhc-hb04 to existing configurations provided that the halui, motion,\n"
"and axis.N pins needed are not otherwise claimed. Instructions are\n"
"included in README file in the directory named above.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:299
msgid ""
"Use halcmd to display the pins and signals used by the xhc-hb04.tcl script:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: src/man/man1/xhc-hb04.1.adoc:304
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  halcmd show pin xhc-hb04       (show all xhc-hb04 pins)\n"
"  halcmd show pin pendant_util   (show all pendant_util pins)\n"
"  halcmd show sig pendant:       (show all pendant signals)\n"
msgstr ""

