#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_clock_set_period.3rtapi.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*rtapi_clock_set_period* sets the basic time interval for realtime tasks.\n"
"All periodic tasks will run at an integer multiple of this period.\n"
"The first call to *rtapi_clock_set_period* with _nsec_ greater than zero will start the clock,\n"
"using _nsec_ as the clock period in nano-seconds.\n"
"Due to hardware and RTOS limitations, the actual period may not be exactly what was requested.\n"
"On success, the function will return the actual clock period if it is available,\n"
"otherwise it returns the requested period. If the requested period is outside the limits\n"
"imposed by the hardware or RTOS, it returns *-EINVAL* and does not start\n"
"the clock. Once the clock is started, subsequent calls with non-zero\n"
"_nsec_ return *-EINVAL* and have no effect.\n"
"Calling *rtapi_clock_set_period* with _nsec_ set to zero queries the clock,\n"
"returning the current clock period, or zero if the clock has not yet been started.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_clock_set_period.3rtapi.adoc:38
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_slab.3rtapi.adoc:32
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_string.3rtapi.adoc:30
msgid ""
"Call only from within init/cleanup code, not from realtime tasks.  This "
"function is not available from non-realtime code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man3/rtapi_clock_set_period.3rtapi.adoc:42
msgid ""
"The actual period provided by the RTOS, which may be different than the "
"requested period, or a RTAPI status code."
msgstr ""

