#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:6
#, fuzzy
msgid "encoder - software counting of quadrature encoder signals"
msgstr "(((encoder))) Conteo por software de señales de encoder en cuadratura."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:10
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*loadrt encoder* [ **num_chan=**__num__ | **names=**__name1__[,_name2_...] ]\n"
msgstr "not [count=n] | [nombres=nombre1[,nombre2...]]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*encoder* is used to measure position by counting the pulses generated\n"
"by a quadrature encoder. As a software-based implementation it is much\n"
"less expensive than hardware, but has a limited maximum count rate. The\n"
"limit is in the range of 10 kHz to 50 kHz, depending on the computer\n"
"speed and other factors. If better performance is needed, a hardware\n"
"encoder counter is a better choice. Some hardware-based systems can\n"
"count at MHz rates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*encoder* supports a maximum of eight channels. The number of channels\n"
"actually loaded is set by the *num_chan* argument when the module is loaded.\n"
"Alternatively, specify names= and unique names separated by commas.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:28
msgid ""
"The *num_chan=* and *names=* specifiers are mutually exclusive. If neither "
"*num_chan=* nor *names=* are specified, or if *num_chan=0* is specified, the "
"default value is three."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*encoder* has a one-phase, unidirectional mode called _counter_. In this\n"
"mode, the *phase-B* input is ignored; the counts increase on each rising\n"
"edge of *phase-A*. This mode may be useful for counting a unidirectional\n"
"spindle with a single input line, though the noise-resistant\n"
"characteristics of quadrature are lost.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:39
msgid ""
"If used in counter-mode it is also possible to enable the missing-teeth "
"index mode, where a gap in the pulse train of one or more teeth is used as "
"in index marker. This system is used extensively for automotive crank "
"position sensors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:42
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*encoder.update-counters* (no floating-point)"
msgstr "'(funct) encoder.update-counters' - Función de alta velocidad para contar pulsos (sin punto flotante)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:47
msgid ""
"Does the actual counting, by sampling the encoder signals and decoding the "
"quadrature waveforms. Must be called as frequently as possible, preferably "
"twice as fast as the maximum desired count rate. Operates on all channels at "
"once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:47
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*encoder.capture-position* (uses floating point)"
msgstr "'lut5' no requiere un hilo de punto flotante."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder.9.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Captures the raw counts from *update-counters* and performs scaling and "
"other necessary conversion, handles counter rollover, etc. Can (and should) "
"be called less frequently than *update-counters*.  Operates on all channels "
"at once."
msgstr ""

