#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder_ratio.9.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*encoder_ratio* can be used to synchronize two axes (like an \"electronic gear\").\n"
"It counts encoder pulses from both axes in software, and\n"
"produces an error value that can be used with a PID loop to make the\n"
"slave encoder track the master encoder with a specific ratio.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder_ratio.9.adoc:21
msgid ""
"This module supports up to eight axis pairs. The number of pairs is set by "
"the module parameter *num_chan*. Alternatively, specify *names=* and unique "
"names separated by commas."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/encoder_ratio.9.adoc:24
msgid ""
"The **num_chan=** and **names=** specifiers are mutually exclusive.  If "
"neither **num_chan=** nor **names=** are specified, the default value is one."
msgstr ""

