#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:1
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "hal_parport(9)"
msgstr "parport"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:7
msgid ""
"hal_parport - Realtime HAL component to communicate with one or more pc "
"parallel ports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:11
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "**loadrt hal_parport cfg=\"**__port_addr__ [_type_] [ [__port_addr__ [__type__] .. .]**\"**\n"
msgstr "loadrt hal_parport cfg=\"port [type] [port [type] ...]\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:18
msgid ""
"The hal_parport component is a realtime component that provides connections "
"from HAL via halpins to the physical pins of one or more parallel ports. It "
"provides a read and write function to send and receive data to the attached "
"parallel port(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:20
msgid "The hal_parport component supports up to **8** physical parallel ports."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:23
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*cfg=\"port_addr [type] [[port_addr [type] ...]\"*"
msgstr "loadrt hal_parport cfg=\"port [type] [port [type] ...]\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:27
msgid ""
"The cfg string tells hal_parport the address(es) of the parallel port(s) and "
"whether the port(s) is/are used as an input or output port(s). Up to eight "
"parallel ports are supported by the component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:33
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The **port_addr **parameter of the configuration string may be either the "
"physical base address of a parallel port or specified as the detected "
"parallel port via Linux parport_pc driver. In which case, a **port_addr** of "
"__0 __is the first parallel port detected on the system, __1__ is the next, "
"and so on."
msgstr ""
"Los números inferiores a 16 se refieren a puertos paralelos detectados por "
"el sistema. Este es la forma más simple de configurar el controlador "
"hal_parport, y coopera con el driver Linux parport_pc, si está cargado. El "
"puerto 0 es el primer puerto paralelo detectado en el sistema, 1 es el "
"siguiente, y así sucesivamente."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:37
msgid ""
"The **type **parameter of the configuration string determines how the I/O "
"bits of the port are used. There are four possible options and if none is "
"specified will default to out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "_in_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:39
msgid ""
"Sets the 8 bits of the data port to input. In this mode the parallel port "
"has a total of 13 input pins and 4 output pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "_out_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Sets the 8 bits of the data port to output. In this mode the parallel port "
"has a total of 5 input pins and 12 output pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "_epp_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:44
msgid ""
"This option is the same as setting to out, but can cause the computer to "
"change the electrical characteristics of the port, see USAGE below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "_x_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:46
msgid ""
"The option allows ports with open collectorts on the control group pins to "
"be configured as inputs resulting in 8 output pins and 9 input pins, see "
"USAGE below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hal_parport.9.adoc:51
msgid ""
"The pins created by the hal_parport component depends on how it is "
"configured in the **cfg=\"\" **string passed to it, see OPTIONS."
