#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:28
msgid ""
"hm2_eth is a device driver that interfaces Mesa's ethernet based Anything I/"
"O boards (with the HostMot2 firmware) to the LinuxCNC HAL.  The supported "
"boards are: 7I76E, 7I80DB, 7I80HD, 7I92, 7I93, 7I94, 7I95, 7I96, 7I96S, "
"7I97, 7I98. It also supports boards with the litehm2 firmware (https://"
"github.com/sensille/litehm2). The board must have its firmware loaded on the "
"board by the mesaflash(1) program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:30
msgid ""
"hm2_eth is only available when LinuxCNC is configured with \"uspace\" "
"realtime."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:31 src/man/man9/hm2_rpspi.9.adoc:83
#: src/man/man9/hm2_spi.9.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "INTERFACE CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:36
msgid ""
"hm2_eth should be used on a dedicated network interface, with only a cable "
"between the PC and the board. Wireless and USB network interfaces are not "
"suitable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:43
msgid ""
"These instructions assume your dedicated network interface is \"eth1\", "
"192.168.1/24 is an unused private network, that the hostmot2 board is using "
"the default address of 192.168.1.121, that you are using Debian 7 or "
"similar, and that you do not otherwise use iptables. If any of these are "
"false, you will need to modify the instructions accordingly. After following "
"all the instructions, reboot so that the changes take effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:52
msgid ""
"It is particularly important to check that the network 192.168.1/24 is not "
"already the private network used by your internet router, because this is a "
"commonly-used value. If you use another network, you will also need to "
"reconfigure the hostmot2 card to use an IP address on that network by using "
"the mesaflash(1) utility and change jumper settings.  Typically, you will "
"choose one of the networks in the https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"IPv4#Private_networks[Private IPv4 address space.] One common alternative is "
"PC address 10.10.10.1, hostmot2 address 10.10.10.10."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:56
msgid ""
"Use of the dedicated ethernet interface while LinuxCNC is running can cause "
"violation of realtime guarantees. hm2_eth will automatically mitigate most "
"accidental causes of interference."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure network with static address"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:61
msgid ""
"Add these lines to the file /etc/network/interfaces to configure the "
"Ethernet interface eth1 with a static address:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"auto eth1\n"
"iface eth1 inet static\n"
"    address 192.168.1.1\n"
"    hardware-irq-coalesce-rx-usecs 0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKET LOSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:79
msgid ""
"While ethernet is fairly resistant to electrical noise, many systems will "
"not have 100% perfect packet reception. The hm2_eth driver has a limited "
"ability to deal with lost packets. Packet loss is detected by transmitting "
"an expected read or write packet count with each request, and checking the "
"value with each read response. When a lost packet is detected, the *packet-"
"error* pin is asserted in that cycle, the *packet-error-level* pin is "
"increased, and if it reaches a threshold then a permanent low-level I/O "
"error is signaled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:85
msgid ""
"However, not all hm2 special functions know how to properly recover from "
"lost packets. For instance, the encoder special function does not properly "
"manage the index feature when packets are lost. The author believes that "
"this can lead to rare failures in home-to-index, which can have severe "
"consequences."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:94
msgid ""
"On the other hand, pid-stepper systems will run properly for extended "
"periods of time with packet loss on the order of .01%, as long as following "
"error is increased enough that having stale position feedback does not "
"trigger a following error. Altering the HAL configuration so that during "
"transient packet loss the pid and motion feedback value is equal to the "
"command value, instead of the stale feedback value, appears to improve "
"tuning. This can be accomplished with a *mux2(9)* component for each "
"feedback signal, using *packet-error* as the mux2 *sel* input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:99
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In addition to the pins documented in *hostmot2(9)*, *hm2_eth(9)* creates "
"the following additional pins:"
msgstr "Además de los pines de salida, hay tres pines de control:"

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "(bit, out) hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.packet-error"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:103
msgid ""
"This pin is TRUE when the most recent cycle detected a read or write error, "
"and FALSE at other times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "(s32, out) hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.packet-error-level"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:107
msgid ""
"This pin shows the current error level, with higher numbers indicating a "
"greater number of recent detected errors. The error level is always in the "
"range from 0 to packet-error-limit, inclusive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "(bit, out) hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.packet-error-exceeded"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:110
msgid ""
"This pin is TRUE when the current error level is equal to the maximum, and "
"FALSE at other times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:115
msgid ""
"In addition to the parameters documented in *hostmot2(9)*, *hm2_eth(9)* "
"creates the following additional parameters:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.packet-error-decrement (s32, rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:119
msgid ""
"The amount deducted from _packet-error-level_ in a cycle without detected "
"read or write errors, without going below zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.packet-error-increment (s32, rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:122
msgid ""
"The amount added to _packet-error-level_ in a cycle without detected read or "
"write errors, without going above packet-error-limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.packet-error-limit (s32, rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:126
msgid ""
"The level at which a detected read or write error is treated as a permanent "
"error. When this error level is reached, the board's _io-error_ pin becomes "
"TRUE and the condition must be manually reset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "hm2__<BoardType>_._<BoardNum>_.packet-read-timeout (s32, rw)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:133
msgid ""
"The length of time that must pass before a read request times out. If the "
"value is less than or equal to 0, it is interpreted as 80% of the thread "
"period. If the value is less than 100, it is interpreted as a percentage of "
"the thread period. Otherwise, it is interpreted as a time in nanoseconds. In "
"any case, the timeout is never less than 100 microseconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:136
msgid ""
"Setting this value too low can cause spurious read errors. Setting it too "
"high can cause realtime delay errors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:149
msgid ""
"hm2_eth uses an iptables chain called \"hm2-eth-rules-output. That "
"technology is common to control network access to (INPUT chain), through "
"(FORWARD chain) or from (OUTPUT chain) your computer. Someone who has "
"configured a firewall on Linux has encountered iptables and is familiar with "
"that technology. This chain contains additional rules to control network "
"interface while HAL is running. The chain is created if it does not exist, "
"and a jump to it is inserted at the beginning of the OUTPUT chain if it is "
"not there already. If you have an existing iptables setup, you can insert a "
"direct jump from OUTPUT to hm2-eth-rules-output in an order appropriate to "
"your local network."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:153
msgid ""
"At (normal) exit, hm2_eth will remove the rules. After a crash, you can "
"manually clear the rules with *sudo iptables -F hm2-eth-rules-output*; the "
"rules are also removed by a reboot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:159
msgid ""
"\"hardware-irq-coalesce-rx-usecs\" decreases time waiting to receive a "
"packet on most systems, but on at least some Marvel-chipset NICs it is "
"harmful.  If the line does not improve system performance, then remove it.  "
"A reboot is required for the value to be set back to its power-on default.  "
"This requires the ethtool package to be installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:164
msgid ""
"Some hostmot2 functions such uart are coded in a way that causes additional "
"latency when used with hm2_eth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:169
msgid ""
"On the 7i92, the HAL pins for the LEDs are called CR01..CR04, but the "
"silkscreens are CR3..CR6. Depending on the FPGA firmware, the LEDs may "
"initially be under control of the ethernet engine. This can be changed until "
"power cycle with"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "elbpcom 01D914000000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:177
msgid ""
"Depending on firmware version, this driver may cause the hardware error LED "
"to light even though the driver and hardware are functioning normally. This "
"will reportedly be fixed in future bitfile updates from Mesa."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_eth.9.adoc:181
#, fuzzy
msgid "hostmot2(9), elbpcom(1)"
msgstr "hostmot2"

