#, no-wrap
msgid "p: (Pad)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:497
msgid ""
"Does not create any pins, used to ignore sections of the bit stream that are "
"not required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:497
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "b: (Boolean)."
msgstr "Parámetros debounce"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:502
msgid ""
"(bit, out) hm2_XXXX.N.ssi.MM.<name>. If any bits in the designated field "
"width are non-zero then the HAL pin will be \"True\". (bit, out)  hm2_XXXX.N."
"ssi.MM.<name>-not. An inverted version of the above, the HAL pin will be "
"\"True\" if all bits in the field are zero."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:502 src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:574
#, no-wrap
msgid "u: (Unsigned)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:508
msgid ""
"(float, out) hm2_XXXX.N.ssi.MM.<name>. The value of the bits interpreted as "
"an unsigned integer then scaled such that the pin value will equal the "
"scalemax parameter value when all bits are high. (for example if the field "
"is 8 bits wide and the scalmax parameter was 20 then a value of 255 would "
"return 20, and 0 would return 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:508 src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:577
#, no-wrap
msgid "s: (Signed)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:512
msgid ""
"(float, out) hm2_XXXX.N.ssi.MM.<name>. The value of the bits interpreted as "
"a 2s complement signed number then scaled similarly to the unsigned variant, "
"except symmetrical around zero."
