#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "scale (float, read/write)"
msgstr "(float) *scale*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:693
msgid ""
"The position scale, in machine units per resolver electrical revolution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:693
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "velocity-scale (float, read/write)"
msgstr "(float) *scale*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:697
msgid ""
"The conversion factor between resolver rotation speed and machine velocity. "
"A value of 1 will typically give motor speed in RPS, a value of 0.01666667 "
"will give (approximate) RPM."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:697
#, no-wrap
msgid "index-divisor (default 1) (u32, read/write)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:707
msgid ""
"The resolver component emulates an index at a fixed point in the sin/cos "
"cycle. Some resolvers have multiple cycles per rev (often related to the "
"number of pole-pairs on the attached motor). LinuxCNC requires an index once "
"per revolution for proper threading etc. This parameter should be set to the "
"number of cycles per rev of the resolver. CAUTION: Which pseudo-index is "
"used will not necessarily be consistent between LinuxCNC runs. Do not expect "
"to re-start a thread after restarting LinuxCNC. It is not appropriate to use "
"this parameter for index-homing of axis drives."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:707
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "excitation-khz (float, read/write)"
msgstr "(float) *scale*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hostmot2.9.adoc:716
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This pin sets the excitation frequency for the resolver. This pin is\n"
"module-level rather than instance-level as all resolvers share the\n"
"same excitation frequency. Valid values are 10 (~10 kHz), 5 (~5 kHz)\n"
"and 2.5 (~2.5 kHz). The actual frequency depends on the FPGA\n"
"frequency, and they correspond to CLOCK_LOW/5000, CLOCK_LOW/10000 and\n"
"CLOCK_LOW/20000 respectively. The parameter will be set to the closest\n"
"available of the three frequencies. A value of -1 (the default)\n"
"indicates that the current setting should be retained.\n"
msgstr ""

