#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:54
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "**siggen.**_N_**.reset** bit in"
msgstr "'lut5' no requiere un hilo de punto flotante."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:56
msgid ""
"Resets output pins to pretermined states: sine 0 sawtooth 0 square -1 * "
"amplitude cosine -1 * amplitude triangle -1 * amplitude"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:56
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "**siggen.**_N_**.clock** bit out"
msgstr "'encoder.<chan>.counts-latched' (s32, salida) - No se usa en este momento."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:58
msgid ""
"The clock output. Bit type clock signal output at the commanded frequency."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:58
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "**siggen.**_N_**.square** float out"
msgstr "'encoder.<chan>.position-latched (float, salida)' - No utilizado en este momento."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:61
msgid ""
"The square wave output. Positive while *triangle* and *cosine* are ramping "
"upwards, and while *sine* is negative."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:61
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "**siggen.**_N_**.sine** float out"
msgstr "'encoder.<chan>.position-latched (float, salida)' - No utilizado en este momento."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:63
msgid "The sine output. Lags *cosine* by 90 degrees."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:63
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "**siggen.**_N_**.cosine** float out"
msgstr "'encoder.<chan>.position-latched (float, salida)' - No utilizado en este momento."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:65
msgid "The cosine output. Leads *sine* by 90 degrees."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:65
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "**siggen.**_N_**.triangle** float out"
msgstr "'encoder.<chan>.position-latched (float, salida)' - No utilizado en este momento."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/siggen.9.adoc:69
msgid ""
"The triangle wave output.  Ramps up while *square* is positive, and down "
"while *square* is negative.  Reaches its positive and negative peaks at the "
"same time as *cosine*."
