#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "TIMING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:168
msgid ""
"There are five timing parameters which control the output waveform. No step "
"type uses all five, and only those which will be used are exported to HAL. "
"The values of these parameters are in nano-seconds, so no recalculation is "
"needed when changing thread periods. In the timing diagrams that follow, "
"they are identified by the following numbers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:170
msgid "{empty}(1) *stepgen.n.steplen*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:172
msgid "{empty}(2) *stepgen.n.stepspace*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:174
msgid "{empty}(3) *stepgen.n.dirhold*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:176
msgid "{empty}(4) *stepgen.n.dirsetup*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:178
msgid "{empty}(5) *stepgen.n.dirdelay*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:182
msgid ""
"For step type 0, timing parameters 1 thru 4 are used. The following timing "
"diagram shows the output waveforms, and what each parameter adjusts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:186
msgid ""
"For step type 1, timing parameters 1, 2, and 5 are used. The following "
"timing diagram shows the output waveforms, and what each parameter adjusts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:193
msgid ""
"For step types 2 and higher, the exact pattern of the outputs depends on the "
"step type (see the HAL manual for a full listing). The outputs change from "
"one state to another at a minimum interval of *steplen*.  When a direction "
"change occurs, the minimum time between the last step in one direction and "
"the first in the other direction is the sum of *steplen* and *dirdelay*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:196
msgid "The HAL User Manual."
msgstr ""

