#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man9/threads.9.adoc:1
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "threads(9)"
msgstr "threads"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/threads.9.adoc:6
#, fuzzy
msgid "threads - creates hard realtime HAL threads"
msgstr "(((threads)))Crea hilos HAL en tiempo real."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/threads.9.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "**loadrt threads name1=_name_** **period1=**_period_ [**fp1**=<**0**|**1**>] [<_thread-2-info_>] [<_thread-3-info_>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/threads.9.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*threads* is used to create hard realtime threads which can execute HAL\n"
"functions at specific intervals. It is not a true HAL component, in that\n"
"it does not export any functions, pins, or parameters of its own. Once\n"
"it has created one or more threads, the threads stand alone, and the\n"
"*threads* component can be unloaded without affecting them. In fact, it\n"
"can be unloaded and then reloaded to create additional threads, as many\n"
"times as needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/threads.9.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*threads* can create up to three realtime threads. Threads must be\n"
"created in order, from fastest to slowest. Each thread is specified by\n"
"three arguments. *name1* is used to specify the name of the first thread\n"
"(thread 1). *period1* is used to specify the period of thread 1 in\n"
"nanoseconds. Both _name_ and _period_ are required. The third argument,\n"
"*fp1* is optional, and is used to specify if thread 1 will be used to\n"
"execute floating point code. If not specified, it defaults to *1*, which\n"
"means that the thread will support floating point. Specify *0* to\n"
"disable floating point support, which saves a small amount of execution\n"
"time by not saving the FPU context. For additional threads, *name2*,\n"
"*period2*, *fp2*, *name3*, *period3*, and *fp3* work exactly the same.\n"
"If more than three threads are needed, unload threads, then reload it to\n"
"create more threads.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/threads.9.adoc:54
msgid ""
"The existence of *threads* might be considered a bug. Ideally, creation and "
"deletion of threads would be done directly with *halcmd* commands, such as "
"\"*newthread *_name period_\", \"*delthread *_name_\", or similar.  However, "
"limitations in the current HAL implementation require thread creation to "
"take place in kernel space, and loading a component is the most "
"straightforward way to do that."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man9/watchdog.9.adoc:1
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "watchdog(9)"
msgstr "watchdog"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/watchdog.9.adoc:6
#, fuzzy
msgid "watchdog - monitor multiple inputs for a \"heartbeat\""
msgstr ""
"(((watchdog))) Monitorea de una a treinta y dos entradas para un 'latido'."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/watchdog.9.adoc:10
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*loadrt watchdog num_inputs=*__N__\n"
