#. type: Title ==
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:150
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Non-trivial kinematics"
msgstr "Cinemática no trivial"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:158
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There can be quite a few types of machine setups (robots: puma, scara; "
"hexapods etc.). Each of them is set up using linear and rotary joints.  "
"These joints don't usually match with the Cartesian coordinates, therefore "
"we need a kinematics function which does the conversion (actually 2 "
"functions: forward and inverse kinematics function)."
msgstr ""
"Puede haber bastantes tipos de configuraciones de máquina (robots: puma, "
"scara; hexápodos, etc.). Cada uno de ellos se configura utilizando "
"articulacions lineales y giratorias.  Estas articulaciones generalmente no "
"coinciden con las coordenadas cartesianas y, por lo tanto, necesitamos una "
"función cinemática que haga la conversión (en realidad 2 funciones: "
"cinemática directa e inversa)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:162
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To illustrate the above, we will analyze a simple kinematics called bipod (a "
"simplified version of the tripod, which is a simplified version of the "
"hexapod)."
msgstr ""
"Para ilustrar lo anterior, analizaremos una maquina de cinemática simple "
"llamada bípode (una versión simplificada del trípode, que es una version "
"simplificada del hexápodo)."

#. type: Positional ($1) AttributeList argument for macro 'image'
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:163 src/motion/kinematics.adoc:164
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Bipod setup"
msgstr "Configuración del bípode"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:164
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/bipod.png"
msgstr "images/bipod.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:170
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Bipod we are talking about is a device that consists of 2 motors placed "
"on a wall, from which a device is hung using some wire. The joints in this "
"case are the distances from the motors to the device (named AD and BD in the "
"figure)."
msgstr ""
"El Bipod del que estamos hablando es un dispositivo que consta de 2 motores "
"colocado en una pared, de la cual cuelga un dispositivo usando un cable. Las "
"articulaciones en este caso son las distancias desde los motores al "
"dispositivo (llamadas AD y BD en la figura)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:175
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The position of the motors is fixed by convention. Motor A is in (0,0), "
"which means that its X coordinate is 0, and its Y coordinate is also 0. "
"Motor B is placed in (Bx, 0), which means that its X coordinate is Bx."
msgstr ""
"La posición de los motores está fijada por convención. El motor A está en "
"(0,0), lo que significa que su coordenada X es 0, y su coordenada Y es "
"también 0. El motor B se coloca en (Bx, 0), lo que significa que su "
"coordenada X es Bx (y a la misma altura Y que el otro motor)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:178
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Our tooltip will be in point D which gets defined by the distances AD and "
"BD, and by the Cartesian coordinates Dx, Dy."
msgstr ""
"Nuestra herramienta estará en el punto D que se define por las distancias AD "
"y BD, y por las coordenadas cartesianas Dx, Dy."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:181
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The job of the kinematics is to transform from joint lengths (AD, BD)  to "
"Cartesian coordinates (Dx, Dy) and vice-versa."
msgstr ""
"El trabajo de la cinemática es transformar a partir de longitudes de "
"articulaciones (AD, BD) a coordenadas cartesianas (Dx, Dy) y viceversa."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:188
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To transform from joint space into Cartesian space we will use some "
"trigonometry rules (the right triangles determined by the points (0,0), "
"(Dx,0), (Dx,Dy) and the triangle (Dx,0), (Bx,0) and (Dx,Dy))."
msgstr ""
"Para transformar del espacio de articulaciones al espacio cartesiano "
"utilizaremos algunas reglas de trigonometría (los triángulos rectángulos "
"determinados por los puntos (0,0), (Dx, 0), (Dx, Dy) y el triángulo (Dx, 0), "
"(Bx, 0) y (Dx, Dy))."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:190
#, fuzzy
msgid "We can easily see that:"
msgstr "Podemos ver fácilmente que:"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:191
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-01.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-01.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:194
#, fuzzy
msgid "likewise:"
msgstr "asi como:"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:195
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-02.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-02.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:198
#, fuzzy
msgid "If we subtract one from the other we will get:"
msgstr "Si restamos una de la otra obtendremos:"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:199
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-03.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-03.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:202
#, fuzzy
msgid "and therefore:"
msgstr "y por lo tanto:"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:203
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-04.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-04.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:206
#, fuzzy
msgid "From there we calculate:"
msgstr "A partir de ahí calculamos:"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:207
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-05.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-05.png"

#. we can easily see that latexmath:[$AD^{2}=x^{2}+y^{2}$], likewise
#. latexmath:[$BD^{2}=(Bx-x)^{2}+y^{2}$].
#. If we subtract one from the other we will get:
#. latexmath::[\[AD^{2}-BD^{2}=x^{2}+y^{2}-x^{2}+2*x*Bx-Bx^{2}-y^{2}\]]
#. and therefore:
#. latexmath::[\[x=\frac{AD^{2}-BD^{2}+Bx^{2}}{2*Bx}\]]
#. From there we calculate:
#. latexmath::[\[y=\sqrt{AD^{2}-x^{2}}\]]
#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:231
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Note that the calculation for y involves the square root of a difference, "
"which may not result in a real number. If there is no single Cartesian "
"coordinate for this joint position, then the position is said to be a "
"singularity. In this case, the forward kinematics return -1."
msgstr ""
"Tenga en cuenta que el cálculo para y implica la raíz cuadrada de una "
"diferencia, que puede dar como resultado un número no real. Si no hay una "
"sola coordenada cartesiana para esta posición de articulacion, la posición "
"se dice que es una singularidad. En este caso, la cinemática directa retorna "
"-1."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:233
#, fuzzy
msgid "Translated to actual code:"
msgstr "Traducido al código actual:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:243
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"double AD2 = joints[0] * joints[0];\n"
"double BD2 = joints[1] * joints[1];\n"
"double x = (AD2 - BD2 + Bx * Bx) / (2 * Bx);\n"
"double y2 = AD2 - x * x;\n"
"if(y2 < 0) return -1;\n"
"pos->tran.x = x;\n"
"pos->tran.y = sqrt(y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"
msgstr ""
"double AD2 = joints[0] * joints[0];\n"
"double BD2 = joints[1] * joints[1];\n"
"double x = (AD2 - BD2 + Bx * Bx) / (2 * Bx);\n"
"double y2 = AD2 - x * x;\n"
"if(y2 < 0) return -1;\n"
"pos->tran.x = x;\n"
"pos->tran.y = sqrt(y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:245
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Inverse transformation"
msgstr "Transformación inversa"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:249
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The inverse kinematics is much easier in our example, as we can write it "
"directly:"
msgstr ""
"La cinemática inversa es mucho más fácil en nuestro ejemplo, ya que podemos "
"escribir directamente"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:250
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-06.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-06.png"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:252
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "images/kinematics-math-07.png"
msgstr "images/kinematics-math-07.png"

#. latexmath::[\[AD=\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}\]]
#. latexmath::[\[BD=\sqrt{(Bx-x)^{2}+y^{2}}\]]
#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:261
#, fuzzy
msgid "or translated to actual code:"
msgstr "or traducido al código real:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/motion/kinematics.adoc:268
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"double x2 = pos->tran.x * pos->tran.x;\n"
"double y2 = pos->tran.y * pos->tran.y;\n"
"joints[0] = sqrt(x2 + y2);\n"
"joints[1] = sqrt((Bx - pos->tran.x)*(Bx - pos->tran.x) + y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"
msgstr ""
"double x2 = pos->tran.x * pos->tran.x;\n"
"double y2 = pos->tran.y * pos->tran.y;\n"
"joints[0] = sqrt(x2 + y2);\n"
"joints[1] = sqrt((Bx - pos->tran.x)*(Bx - pos->tran.x) + y2);\n"
"return 0;\n"

