#. type: Plain text
#: src/motion/pid-theory.adoc:176
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"'Ziegler-Nichols method', introduced by John G. Ziegler and Nathaniel B. "
"Nichols in 1942 footnote:[Ziegler, J. G. and Nichols, N. B. (1942), 'Optimum "
"Settings for Automatic Controllers', Transactions of the ASME, link:https://"
"doi.org/10.1115/1.2899060[DOI 10.1115/1.2899060] and link:https://web."
"archive.org/web/20170918055307/http://staff.guilan.ac.ir/staff/users/"
"chaibakhsh/fckeditor_repo/file/documents/"
"Optimum%20Settings%20for%20Automatic%20Controllers%20(Ziegler%20and%20Nichols,"
"%201942).pdf[The Internet Archive].]. It starts in the same way as the "
"method described before: first set the I and D gains to zero and then "
"increase the P gain and expose the loop to external interference for example "
"knocking the motor axis to cause it to move out of equilibrium in order to "
"determine critical gain and period of oscillation until the output of the "
"loop starts to oscillate.  Write down the critical gain (K~c~) and the "
"oscillation period of the output (P~c~). Then adjust the P, I and D controls "
"as the table shows:"
msgstr ""
"Otro método de ajuste se conoce formalmente como el 'método Ziegler-"
"Nichols', presentado por John G. Ziegler y Nathaniel B. Nichols. Comienza de "
"la misma manera que el método descrito anteriormente: primero, se configura "
"I y D a cero y luego se aumenta la ganancia P y se expone el ciclo a una "
"interferencia externa, por ejemplo golpeando el eje del motor para sacarlo "
"del equilibrio, con el fin de determinar la ganancia crítica y el período de "
"oscilación hasta que la salida del bucle comience a oscilar.  Anote la "
"ganancia crítica (K~c~) y el periodo de la oscilación de la salida (P~c~). "
"Luego ajuste los controles P, I y D como muestra la tabla:"

