#. type: TH
#: man/man9/bldc.9:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "BLDC"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:13
msgid "bldc - BLDC and AC-servo control component"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:15
msgid "B<loadrt bldc cfg=qi6,aH>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:20
msgid ""
"This component is designed as an interface between the most common forms of "
"three-phase motor feedback devices and the corresponding types of drive.  "
"However, there is no requirement that the motor and drive should necessarily "
"be of inherently compatible types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:23
msgid ""
"Each instance of the component is defined by a group of letters describing "
"the input and output types.  A comma separates individual instances of the "
"component. For example B<loadrt bldc cfg=qi6,aH>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: man/man9/bldc.9:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:26
msgid "Input type definitions are all lower-case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:29
msgid ""
"B<n> No motor feedback. This mode could be used to drive AC induction "
"motors, but is also potentially useful for creating free-running motor "
"simulators for drive testing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:33
msgid ""
"B<h> Hall sensor input.  Brushless DC motors (electronically commutated "
"permanent magnet 3-phase motors) typically use a set of three Hall sensors "
"to measure the angular position of the rotor.  A lower-case B<h> in the cfg "
"string indicates that these should be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:37
msgid ""
"B<a> Absolute encoder input. (Also possibly used by some forms of Resolver "
"conversion hardware).  The presence of this tag over-rides all other "
"inputs.  Note that the component still requires to be be connected to the "
"B<rawcounts> encoder pin to prevent loss of commutation on index-reset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:40
msgid ""
"B<q> Incremental (quadrature) encoder input.  If this input is used then the "
"rotor will need to be homed before the motor can be run."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:42
msgid "B<i> Use the index of an incremental encoder as a home reference."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:46
msgid ""
"B<f> Use a 4-bit Gray-scale pattern to determine rotor alignment.  This "
"scheme is only used on the Fanuc \"Red Cap\" motors.  This mode could be "
"used to control one of these motors using a non-Fanuc drive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:48
msgid "Output type descriptions are all upper-case."
