#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:161
msgid ""
"A rising edge on this pin starts the motor alignment sequence.  This pin "
"should be connected in such a way that the motors re-align any time that "
"encoder monitoring has been interrupted.  Typically this will only be at "
"machine power-off.  The alignment process involves powering the motor phases "
"in such a way as to put the motor in a known position.  The encoder counts "
"are then stored in the B<offset> parameter.  The alignment process will tend "
"to cause a following error if it is triggered while the axis is enabled, so "
"should be set before the matching axis.N.enable pin.  The complementary "
"B<init-done> pin can be used to handle the required sequencing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/bldc.9:164
msgid ""
