#. type: TH
#: man/man9/carousel.9:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "CAROUSEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:13
msgid "carousel - Orient a toolchanger carousel using various encoding schemes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:19
msgid ""
"B<loadrt carousel pockets=>I<N>[,I<N>] B<encoding=>I<ssss>[,I<sss>] "
"B<num_sense=>I<N>[,I<N>] B<dir=>I<N>[,I<N]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/man9/carousel.9:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<pockets> The number of pockets in each toolchanger."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:24
msgid ""
"Use up to 8 numbers separated by commas to create multiple carousel "
"components."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/man9/carousel.9:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<encoding> The position encoding."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:27
msgid "gray, binary, bcd, index, edge, counts or single. Default = 'gray'"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: man/man9/carousel.9:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<num_sense> The number of position sense pins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:30
#, fuzzy
msgid "Default = 4."
msgstr "Los valores predeterminados son:"

#. type: TP
#: man/man9/carousel.9:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<dir> Set to 1 for unidirectional or  2 for bidirectional operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:33
#, fuzzy
msgid "Default = bidirectional"
msgstr "Valores predeterminados y opciones"

#. type: TP
#: man/man9/carousel.9:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<parity> Set to 1 for odd parity, 0 for even parity checking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:36
msgid "Default = 0 (even)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:41
msgid ""
"This component is intended to help operate various types of carousel-type "
"toolchangers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:51
msgid ""
"The component can be configured to operate with binary, binary-coded decimal "
"(BCD)  or gray-coded position feedback ('binary;, 'bcd' and 'gray' modes)  "
"It can alternatively work with an individual sensor for each tool position "
"('single' mode) or with a sensor at each tool position and a separate index "
"('index' mode). Systems using a stepper motor or quadrature encoder are also "
"supported ('counts' mode).  B<edge> is a special case of index mode for tool "
"changers with pockets on both the rising and falling edges of the position "
"sensor.  (Seen on at least one Denford Orac.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:54
msgid ""
"Both unidirectional and bidirectional systems are supported and those that "
"reverse against a stop when in position."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:57
msgid ""
"The number of carousel component instances created depends on the number of "
"entries in the 'pockets' modparam. For example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:59
msgid "B<loadrt carousel pockets=10,10,8>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:63
msgid ""
"Would create 3 carousel instances with 10, 10 and 8 pockets. The other "
"parameters are optional. If absent then defaults will be used. Any missing "
"entry will assume the previous value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:70
msgid ""
"When the enable pin is set to true the component will immediately set the "
"\"active\" pin to true and then (for a bidirectional instance) calculate the "
"shortest path to the requested pocket number. The appropriate motor "
"direction output pins will then be set. Bit outputs for forward and reverse "
"are provided as well as a three-state velocity output for driving a DC motor "
"PWM or a velocity-mode stepgen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:74
msgid ""
"The component will monitor the carousel position and, when the correct "
"position is reached, set the motor-control pins to 0, set \"active\" to 0 "
"and set \"ready\" to 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:82
msgid ""
"In 'index', 'edge' or 'counts'mode there is a need to find the initial home "
"position of the carousel.  The first time that the \"enable\" pin is set; "
"the carousel will rotate forwards searching for a home signal. In 'index' "
"and 'edge' mode this is when both the index and pulse inputs are true. In "
"'counts' mode only the index input needs to be set to set home. Additionally "
"in 'counts' mode the usual index-enable logic of the encoder counters is "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:92
msgid ""
"With some carousel designs the carousel will not stop immediately. To allow "
"for this set the B<lign-dc> pin to a low velocity to be used for a final "
"latching move, and set theB<decel-time> to a suitable value.  Once the decel-"
"time has expired the carousel will, if it was moving forwards, reverse back "
"on to the position marker, off of the arker and then bak on to the FWD edge. "
"If moving in reverse it will continue off the marker and then reverse slowly "
"on to the FWD edge.  This algnment is only possible with a motor-vel "
"controlled bidirectional carousel, Other combinations will be accepted but "
"probably won't have the desired behaviour.  Some tuning will be needed of "
"align-dc and decel-time to achieve reliable operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:95
msgid ""
"In the unusual case that the index and pulse signals do not align it is "
"possible to use HAL logic to achieve the desired pin switching during homing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:100
msgid ""
"Setting \"enable\" low does not halt the homing move, so if homing on first "
"tool change is not needed then the enable pin can be toggled by an axis "
"homing pin or a script and the homing process will continue even if that "
"driving signal resets during the carousel homing move."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:111
msgid ""
"To operate the component with an encoder or stepgen use mode \"C\". The "
"B<scale> pin should be the number of steps or encoder counts between pocket "
"centres. The B<width> pin can be used to stop the motor some distance before "
"the centre of the pocket to allow the motor time to decelerate.  In mode "
"\"C\" it is possible to use either the speed/direction control used in other "
"modes or to use direct position mode using the counts-target pin. The "
"internal scaling of the encoder or stepgen should be set to 1.0. A PID hal "
"component will be needed for encoder applications whereas stepgen "
"configurations can use a stepgen in position control mode or in velocity "
"control mode with a PID."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/carousel.9:116
msgid ""
"For tool changers which lock the carousel against a stop the B<rev-pulse> "
"pin can be set to a non-zero value. The motor-rev pin will then be set for "
"this many seconds at the completion of the tool search and at the same time "
"the reverse duty/cycle velocity value will be sent to the motor-vel pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
