msgstr "and2 [count=N] | [nombres=nombre1[, nombre2 ...]]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/corexy_by_hal.9:22
msgid ""
"Implement B<CoreXY> forward and inverse transformations B<in HAL>.  This "
"component provides an alternative method for implementing B<CoreXY> "
"kinematics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/corexy_by_hal.9:24
#, fuzzy
msgid "In the INI file, use:"
msgstr "Leer el archivo INI"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/corexy_by_hal.9:26
#, fuzzy
msgid "B<[KINS]KINEMATICS=trivkins coordinates=xyz kinstype=both>"
msgstr ""
"[KINS]\n"
"KINEMATICS = trivkins coordinates=xyz kinstype=both\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/corexy_by_hal.9:34
msgid ""
"This component accepts two joint (B<j0,j1>) motor position commands for a "
"trivkins coordinates=xyz configuration and computes equivalent B<CoreXY> "
"motor commands for two motors identified as B<alpha,beta>.  Similarly, the "
"component accepts feedback values for the B<alpha,beta> motor controllers "
"and converts to equivalent joint (B<j0,j1>) motor position feedback values."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/corexy_by_hal.9:39
msgid ""
"1) Using B<trivkins> with this module allows home switches to trigger "
"according to the B<Cartesian x,y> positions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/corexy_by_hal.9:44
msgid ""
"2) Joint pin names are based on B<coordinates=xyz> and the corresponding "
"joint number assignments used by B<trivkins> so B<j0==x, j1==y> (man "
"trivkins for more information)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/corexy_by_hal.9:49
msgid ""
"3) B<CoreXY> kinematics can also be implemented using the kinematics module "
"named B<corexykins> with home switches triggered by the B< j0,j1 motor> "
"positions.  (man kins for more information)"
msgstr ""

