#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:23
msgid ""
"An offset is computed (from one of several functions) based on an input "
"angle in degrees.  The angle could be a rotary coordinate value or a spindle "
"angle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:31
msgid ""
"The computed offset is represented as an s32 B<kcounts> output pin that is a "
"compatible input to external offset pins like B<axis.L.eoffset-counts> where "
"B<L> is the coordinate letter.  Scaling of the s32 B<kcounts> is controlled "
"by the input (B<k>) -- its reciprocal value is presented on an output pin "
"(B<kreciprocal>) for connection to B<axis.L.eoffset-scale>.  The default "
"value for B<k> should be suitable for most uses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:36
msgid ""
"The built-in functions use pins B<fmult> and B<rfraction> to control the "
"output frequency (or number of polygon sides)  and amplitude respectively.  "
"The B<rfraction> pin controls the offset amplitude as a fraction of the "
"B<radius-ref> pin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One of the four built-in functions is specified by the B<fnum> pin:\n"
"  B<0>: f0 inside  polygon  (requires B<fmult> == nsides E<gt>= 3)\n"
"  B<1>: f1 outside polygon  (requires B<fmult> == nsides E<gt>= 3)\n"
"  B<2>: f2 sinusoid\n"
"  B<3>: f3 square wave\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:44
