#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:109
msgid ""
"An example simulation configuration is provided at: B<configs/sim/axis/"
"external_offsets/opa.ini>.  A simulated XZC machine uses the B<C> coordinate "
"angle to offset the transverse B<X> coordinate according to the selected "
"B<fnum> function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:118
msgid ""
"B<radius-ref>: The computed offsets are based on the B<radius-ref> pin "
"value.  This pin may be set to a constant radius value or controlled by a "
"user interface or by g code program (using B<M68> and a B<motion.analog-out-"
"NN pin for instance).>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:125
msgid ""
"B<Stopping>: When the B<enable-in> pin is deasserted, the offset is returned "
"to zero respecting the allocated acceleration and velocity limits.  The "
"allocations for coordinate B<L> are typically controlled by an ini file "
"setting: B<[AXIS_L]OFFSET_AV_RATIO>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/eoffset_per_angle.9:132
msgid ""
"If unsupported parameters are supplied to a function (for instance a polygon "
"with fewer than three sides), the current offset will be returned to zero "
"(respecting velocity and acceleration constraints).  After correcting the "
"offending parameter, the B<enable-in> pin must be toggled to resume offset "
"computations."
msgstr ""

