#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/gantry.9:23
msgid ""
"The `personality' value is the number of joints to control.  Two is typical, "
"but up to seven is supported (a three joint setup has been tested with "
"hardware)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/gantry.9:32
msgid ""
"All controlled joints track the commanded position (with a per-joint offset) "
"unless in the process of homing.  Homing is when the commanded position is "
"moving towards the homing switches (as determined by the sign of search-"
"vel)  and the joint home switches are not all in the same state.  When the "
"system is homing and a joint home switch activates, the command value sent "
"to that joint is \"frozen\" and the joint offset value is updated instead.  "
"Once all home switches are active, there are no more adjustments made to the "
"offset values and all joints run in lock-step once more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/gantry.9:35
msgid ""
"For best results, set HOME_SEARCH_VEL and HOME_LATCH_VEL to the same "
"direction and as slow as practical.  When a joint home switch trips, the "
"commanded velocity will drop immediately from HOME_SEARCH_VEL to zero, with "
"no limit on acceleration."
msgstr ""

