#. type: TH
#: man/man9/lut5.9:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "LUT5"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:13
#, fuzzy
msgid "lut5 - Arbitrary 5-input logic function based on a look-up table"
msgstr ""
"(((lut5)))Función lógica de 5 entradas basada en tabla de consulta (look-up "
"table)."

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:16
#, fuzzy
msgid "B<loadrt lut5 [count=>I<N>B<|names=>I<name1>B<[,>I<name2...>B<]]>"
msgstr "and2 [count=N] | [nombres=nombre1[, nombre2 ...]]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:25
msgid ""
"B<lut5> constructs a logic function with up to 5 inputs using a B<l>ook-"
"B<u>p B<t>able.  The value for B<function> can be determined by writing the "
"truth table, and computing the sum of B<all> the B<weights> for which the "
"output value would be TRUE.  The weights are hexadecimal not decimal so "
"hexadecimal math must be used to sum the weights.  A wiki page has a "
"calculator to assist in computing the proper value for function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:27
#, fuzzy
msgid "https://wiki.linuxcnc.org/cgi-bin/wiki.pl?Lut5"
msgstr "http://wiki.linuxcnc.org/cgi-bin/emcinfo.pl?FixingSMIIssues"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:31
msgid ""
"Note that LUT5 will generate any of the 4,294,967,296 logical functions of 5 "
"inputs so B<AND>, B<OR>, B<NAND>, B<NOR>, B<XOR> and every other "
"combinatorial function is possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/man9/lut5.9:32
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Example Functions"
msgstr "and2 Funciones"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:36
msgid ""
"A 5-input I<and> function is TRUE only when all the inputs are true, so the "
"correct value for B<function> is B<0x80000000>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:39
msgid ""
"A 2-input I<or> function would be the sum of B<0x2> + B<0x4> + B<0x8>, so "
"the correct value for B<function> is B<0xe>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:44
msgid ""
"A 5-input I<or> function is TRUE whenever any of the inputs are true, so the "
"correct value for B<function> is B<0xfffffffe>. Because every weight except "
"B<0x1> is true the function is the sum of every line except the first one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/lut5.9:50
msgid ""
"A 2-input I<xor> function is TRUE whenever exactly one of the inputs is "
"true, so the correct value for B<function> is B<0x6>.  Only B<in-0> and "
"B<in-1> should be connected to signals, because if any other bit is B<TRUE> "
"then the output will be B<FALSE>."
msgstr ""

