#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:32
msgid ""
"matrix_kb - Convert integers to HAL pins\\&. Optionally scan a matrix of I/O "
"ports to create those integers\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:35
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"B<loadrt matrix_kb config=>I<RxCs>,I<RxCs>\\&... B<names=>I<name1>,"
"I<name2>\\&..."
msgstr "and2 [count=N] | [nombres=nombre1[, nombre2 ...]]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:37
msgid ""
"Creates a component configured for R rows and N columns of matrix "
"keyboard\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:39
msgid ""
"If the B<s> option is specified then a set of output rows will be cyclically "
"toggled, and a set of input columns will be scanned\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:41
msgid ""
"The B<names> parameter is optional, but if used then the HAL pins and "
"functions will use the specified names rather than the default ones\\&. This "
"can be useful for readability and 2-pass HAL parsing\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:43
#, fuzzy
msgid "There must be no spaces in the parameter lists\\&."
msgstr "El mismo que se use para pines y parámetros."

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:46
msgid ""
"This component was written to convert matrix keyboard scancodes into HAL "
"pins\\&. However, it might also find uses in converting integers from 0 to "
"I<N> into I<N> HAL pins\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:48
msgid ""
"The component can work in two ways, and the HAL pins created vary according "
"to mode\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:50
msgid ""
"In the default mode the component expects to be given a scan code from a "
"separate driver but could be any integer from any source\\&. Most typically "
"this will be the keypad scancode from a Mesa 7I73\\&. The default codes for "
"keyup and keydown are based on the Mesa 7I73 specification with 0x40 "
"indicating a keydown and 0x80 a keyup event\\&. If using the 7I73 it is "
"important to match the keypad size jumpers with the HAL component\\&. Valid "
"configs for the 7I73 are 4x8 and 8x8\\&. Note that the component will only "
"work properly with the version 12 (0xC) 7I73 firmware\\&. The firmware "
"version is visible on the component parameters in HAL\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:52
msgid ""
"In the optional scan-generation mode the B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.keycode> "
"pin changes to an output pin and a set of output row pins and input column "
"pins are created\\&. These need to be connected to physical inputs and "
"outputs to scan the matrix and return values to HAL\\&. Note the B<negative-"
"logic> parameter described below, this will need to be set on the most "
"common forms of inputs which float high when unconnected\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:54
msgid ""
"In both modes a set of HAL output pins are created corresponding to each "
"node of the matrix\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:57
#, fuzzy
msgid "B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>"
msgstr "match8"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:59
msgid ""
"Perform all requested functions\\&. Should be run in a slow thread for "
"effective debouncing\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:63
msgid "B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.col->I<CC>B<-in> bit in*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:65
msgid "The input pin corresponding to column C\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:68
msgid "B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.key\\&.r>I<R>B<c>I<C> bit out*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:70
msgid "The pin corresponding to the key at row R column C of the matrix\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:73
msgid ""
"B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.keycode> unsigned in or out, depending on mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:75
msgid ""
"This pin should be connected to the scancode generator if hardware such as a "
"7I73 is being used\\&. In this mode it is an input pin\\&. In the internally-"
"generated scanning mode this pin is an output, but will not normally be "
"connected\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:78
#, fuzzy
msgid "B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.row->I<RR>B<-out> bit out*"
msgstr "# setp parport.0.pin-01-out-invert 1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:80
msgid ""
"The row scan drive pins\\&. Should be connected to external hardware pins "
"connected to the keypad\\&. The row scan drive pins\\&.Should be connected "
"to external hardware pins connected to the keypad\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:84
msgid "B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.key_rollover>* unsigned r/w (default 2)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:86
msgid ""
"With most matrix keyboards the scancodes are only unambiguous with 1 or 2 "
"keys pressed\\&. With more keys pressed phantom keystrokes can appear\\&. "
"Some keyboards are optimised to reduce this problem, and some have internal "
"diodes so that any number of keys may be pressed simultaneously\\&. Increase "
"the value of this parameter if such a keyboard is connected, or if phantom "
"keystrokes are more acceptable than only two keys being active at one "
"time\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:89
msgid ""
"B<matrix_kb\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.negative-logic> bit r/w (default 1), only in scan "
"mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/matrix_kb.9:91
msgid ""
"When no keys are pressed a typical digital input will float high\\&. The "
"input will then be pulled low by the keypad when the corresponding poll line "
"is low\\&. Set this parameter to 0 if the I/O in use requires one row at a "
"time to be high, and a high input corresponds to a button press\\&."
msgstr ""

