#, no-wrap
msgid "SIM_PARPORT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:13
msgid ""
"sim_parport - A component to simulate the pins of the hal_parport component"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:16
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"B<loadrt sim_parport [count=>I<N>B<|names=>I<name1>B<[,>I<name2...>B<]]>"
msgstr "and2 [count=N] | [nombres=nombre1[, nombre2 ...]]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:21
msgid ""
"Sim_parport is used to replace the pins of a real parport without changing "
"any of the pins names in the rest of the config."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:23
msgid ""
"It has pass-through pins (ending in -fake) that allows connecting to other "
"components."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:25
msgid "eg pin-02-in will follow pin-02-in-fake 's logic."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:27
msgid ""
"pin_01_out-fake will follow pin_01_out (possibly modified by pin_01_out-"
"invert)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:29
msgid ""
"It creates all possible pins of both 'in' and 'out' options of the "
"hal_parport component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:31
msgid ""
"This allows using other hardware I/O in place of the parport (without having "
"to change the rest of the config)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:33
msgid "or simulating hardware such as limit switches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:35
msgid "it's primary use is in Stepconf for building simulated configs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:37
msgid "You must use the names= option to have the right pin names."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:39
msgid "eg. names=parport.0,parport.1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/sim_parport.9:41
msgid ""
"The read and write functions pass the logic from pins to fake pins or vice "
"vera"
