msgstr "userkins: template for user-built kinematics modules using halcompile"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:25
msgid ""
"The unmodified userkins component can be used as a kinematics file for a "
"machine with identity kinematics for an xyz machine employing 3 joints "
"(motors)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:27
msgid "B<USAGE:>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "  1) Copy the userkins.comp file to a user-owned directory (B<mydir>).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     Note: The userkins.comp file can be downloaded from:\n"
"E<.URL https://github.com/LinuxCNC/linuxcnc/raw/2.8/src/hal/components/userkins.comp>\n"
"     where '2.8' is the branch name (use 'master' for the master branch)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     For a RIP (run-in-place) build, the file is located in\n"
"     the git tree as:\n"
"       src/hal/components/userkins.comp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  2) Edit the functions kinematicsForward() and kinematicsInverse() as required.\n"
"  3) If required, add HAL pins following examples in the template code.\n"
"  4) Build and install the component using halcompile:\n"
"     $ cd B<mydir>\n"
"     $ [sudo] halcompile --install userkins.comp\n"
"     # Note:\n"
"     #      sudo is required when using a deb install\n"
"     #      sudo is B<not> required for run-in-place builds\n"
"     # $ man halcompile for more info\n"
"  5) Specify userkins in an ini file as:\n"
"     B<[KINS]>\n"
"     B<KINEMATICS=userkins>\n"
"     B<JOINTS=3>\n"
"     # the number of JOINTS must agree with the\n"
"     # number of joints used in your modified userkins.comp\n"
"  6) Note: the manpage for userkins is not updated by halcompile --install\n"
"  7) To use a different component name, rename the file (example mykins.comp)\n"
"     and change all instances of 'userkins' to 'mykins'.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"B<NOTES:>\n"
"  1  The B<fpin> pin is included to satisfy the requirements of the\n"
"     halcompile utility but it is not accessible to kinematics functions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/userkins.9:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  2  HAL pins and parameters needed in kinematics functions (kinematicsForward(),\n"
"     kinematicsInverse()) must be setup in a function (B<userkins_setup()>)\n"
"     invoked by the initial motion module call to kinematicsType().\n"
msgstr ""

